    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0202" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg192"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 600.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to report to you that the
                    British government has very liberally acceded to the application made by Mr. P.
                    McD. Collins, and has granted to him the right to continue his proposed
                    telegraph communication from Russia over the English territorial possessions in
                    Northwestern America. Agreeably to the directions contained in your No. 652, of
                    the 13th of July, 1863, I have done whatever was in my power to facilitate his
                    efforts. Mr. Collins is on his way to America, and will report hi ssuccess to
                    you in person.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES ERANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
